# EdgeExpert — Windows Quick Reference

## Architecture (Windows mode)
  Ollama.exe  (Windows host, port 11434)  ← Intel Arc 140T GPU auto
  Open WebUI  (Docker,  port 3000)        ← browser UI
  LiteLLM     (Docker,  port 4000)        ← optional cloud proxy (make win-cloud)

## First-time setup (run once as Admin)
  Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Force
  .\scripts\win-setup.ps1

## Daily commands
  make win-up        # start Open WebUI
  make win-down      # stop
  make win-status    # check containers
  make win-cloud     # start with LiteLLM cloud proxy (Claude/GPT/Gemini in WebUI)

## Ollama (runs on Windows host)
  ollama list
  ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:7b
  ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:14b   # better quality (~9 GB)
  ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:32b   # best (~20 GB, fits in 64 GB RAM)
  ollama rm <model>

## Claude Code (coding agent — installed on Windows)
  # First time: login
  claude login

  # Use in any git repo
  cd C:\path\to\repo
  claude

  # One-shot task
  claude -p "add type hints to utils.py and commit"

## Models path
  C:\ai-data\ollama\models    ← OLLAMA_MODELS (set by win-setup.ps1)
  C:\ai-data\open-webui       ← WebUI database

## Docker Desktop troubleshooting
  # Kill everything and restart
  taskkill /F /IM "Docker Desktop.exe" 2>$null
  taskkill /F /IM "com.docker.backend.exe" 2>$null
  wsl --shutdown
  Stop-Service com.docker.service -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
  Start-Sleep -Seconds 3
  Start-Service com.docker.service
  # Then reopen Docker Desktop from Start Menu

  # Check WSL distros
  wsl -l -v

  # Reset docker-sandbox if needed (run as Admin)
  takeown /F "C:\Program Files\Docker\cli-plugins\docker-sandbox.exe"
  icacls "C:\Program Files\Docker\cli-plugins\docker-sandbox.exe" /grant Administrators:F
  ren "C:\Program Files\Docker\cli-plugins\docker-sandbox.exe" "docker-sandbox.exe.disabled"


